00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.030
Terrible in the sense of
how people are using it.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.520
People think that this product
is great for cleaning ears,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.438
then they go inside their
ears with no training,

00:05:43.438 --> 00:05:46.110
and start scratching up their ear canals,

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.820
busting their tympanic membranes.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:48.870
Yes, their eardrums.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.520
We're seeing this in our offices.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.830
Plus, I don't really
understand the obsession

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.650
of removing earwax from
the inside of your ear.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.483
If it's clogged,

00:05:56.483 --> 00:05:58.200
you could could put eardrops in.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.610
They sell them over the counter.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.200
It'll melt ear wax and it'll come out.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.790
And ear wax is good for your ear.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.950
It actually traps dust, bacteria.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.870
It even protects the canal

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.520
if there's a little moisture in there

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.080
from your skin getting irritated.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.910
There's actually no good medical utility

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.830
that the average person should
have this in their home.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.060
I have it in my home.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.980
I remember when Jen Selter came over

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.710
and she had an earplug
that fell apart in her ear.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.210
And I, as a medical professional,

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.650
was able to use this tool.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.870
But I would not recommend
anyone having this at home.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.970
- [Narrator 3] Remove that
ear wax for better hearing.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.350
- And if your hearing is not good,

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.060
