00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.120
because everyone wants to be taller.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:54.953
Not everyone.

00:06:54.953 --> 00:06:56.340
A lot of people want to be taller.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.460
- [Narrator 4] This posture
corrector is pure magic.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.650
- It depends what your
definition of pure magic is.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.750
It's certainly not my
definition as a doctor.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:07.680
Because posture correctors
largely are unnecessary

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.940
and potentially harmful.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.100
Because the goal of having good posture

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.510
is about creating a good,

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.040
natural posture.
(bell ringing)

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.730
And when you're putting on a
device to create good posture,

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.250
you're essentially weakening the muscles

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.900
that create good posture,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.810
and you become dependent
on a device like this.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.430
There's a lot of information out there

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.740
about, "Posture needs to be perfect."

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.020
You don't always need to
sit up perfectly like this.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.750
Like, it's okay to lean
back if you're tired.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:38.400
But it's about having good
solid strength for your posture

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.440
in order for you to be
able to sit comfortably

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.050
and not have to slouch over like this.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:45.270
Or have a forward
shoulder rounded posture.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.640
So like, these things are far from magic,

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.227
and actually in many cases
do more harm than good.

00:07:50.227 --> 00:07:52.177
"Mastic has been grown in Greece

